title: Raritan PX2/PX3: Whole-Inlet Residual Current
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/environment/raritan
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check reads native residual-current and RCM sensors for each whole inlet
 from the PDU2-MIB inletSensorMeasurementsTable. Inlet-pole measurements are
 handled independently by raritan_pdu_residual_current and are never added
 together or used as replacements for whole-inlet data.

 Combined, AC and DC residual currents have separate metrics. Enabled device
 thresholds, precision, signed values and RCM states are handled by the same
 evaluation as the inlet-pole check. A sole active upper device limit X becomes
 WARN/CRIT X/X. Device WARN 0 with active CRIT X also uses X/X. Explicit rule
 values remain unchanged and take precedence, including zero or disabled levels.
 Rules and metrics use amperes; service output displays milliamperes.

 Both checks use the residual_current rule and its missing-data/missing-levels
 options. Unavailable optional sensors remain excluded. A normal available RCM
 sensor can still result in OK without available numeric residual sensors.
 The percentage metric uses load current from this exact inlet.

item:
 {{Summary}} for the standard PDU 1/inlet 1 case. Other whole-inlet items use
 {{Inlet <ID>}}, with the PDU index added when multiple PDUs are detected.
 Existing service names such as {{Residual Current Summary}} and
 {{Residual Current Inlet 1}} are retained.

discovery:
 One service for each inlet with an available residual-current or RCM sensor.
 No placeholder service is created without such sensors.
